.TH LCOS-NOTES-CLI 1 "October 2026" "LCOS Notes 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lcos-notes-cli \- query and modify a local Markdown vault
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lcos-notes-cli COMMAND VAULT
.RI [ ARGUMENTS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
All successful commands emit one UTF-8 JSON value and a newline.
VAULT must be a directory; note arguments are vault-relative .md paths.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B notes VAULT
List notes in path byte order.
.TP
.B links VAULT NOTE
List wikilinks with Unicode line/column positions and resolved paths.
.TP
.B mdlinks VAULT NOTE
List local inline Markdown note links as raw, text, path, heading, line, col and
resolved. Paths are percent-decoded UTF-8; heading is null without a hash.
Images, titles, reference-style and non-local links are excluded.
.TP
.B resolve VAULT SOURCE INNER
Resolve a wikilink's inner text from SOURCE.
.TP
.B switch VAULT QUERY
List up to 50 notes ranked by a case-folded subsequence query.
.TP
.B create VAULT TARGET
Create an empty note or return an existing resolved note.
.TP
.B tags VAULT
List tags and per-note counts.
.TP
.B tagged VAULT TAG
List notes containing TAG or its nested tags.
.TP
.B find VAULT QUERY
Find up to 500 non-overlapping case-insensitive matches with path, line,
Unicode column and line text. Matches stay within one line, excluding its newline
and final carriage return. Newline queries match nothing. Empty queries are refused.
.TP
.B backlinks VAULT NOTE
List incoming wikilinks and Markdown note links from other notes.
.TP
.B rename VAULT OLD NEW
Move a note and repair affected resolved links, preserving other bytes.
.TP
.B render VAULT NOTE
Render CommonMark with text, style spans and followable note links. Offsets are zero-based
Unicode code points; ranges exclude their end. Frontmatter is omitted.
.TP
.B blocks VAULT NOTE
List top-level CommonMark blocks as objects with line and offset. The line is
1-based in the original file, including removed frontmatter. The offset is a
0-based Unicode code point position in the same text returned by render.
Invalid UTF-8 notes are refused.
.SH LINK RULES
Markdown paths resolve relative to the source folder, then the vault root,
trying each path with and without an appended .md. A leading slash uses only
the vault root. Dot segments collapse without escaping the vault. Matching uses
NFC normalization followed by Unicode case folding; exact path bytes win ties.
Name and tag comparisons also normalize to NFC; search text does not.
Rename preserves Markdown link text, heading, angle form and extension preference,
escaping percent and path hashes and, outside angles, spaces and parentheses.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 2 on refusal, with a single refused: reason line on standard error.
Unsafe creation targets and invalid note paths are refused. Invalid UTF-8 notes
are ignored by search, tags and backlinks and refused by render and rename.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lcos-notes (1)
